-- title:
--   Cancelling powers of λ inside ℚ[λ]
-- statement:
--   Write $\lambda =$ `lambdaModC ℚ` for the Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ obtained by applying the coefficientwise ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Q}$ to the integral Laurent series `lambdaInt`, the latter being the product of the monomial $\mathfrak q^1$ with coefficient $1$, the eighth power of the power series `etaProd` regarded as a Laurent series, the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^4$ applied to `etaProd` $^{16}$, and the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^2$ applied to `dedekindEtaUnitInv`. The assertion is: let $w$ be a Laurent series with rational coefficients all of whose coefficients in strictly negative degrees vanish, so that $w$ is a power series in $\mathfrak q$, and let $a$ be a natural number. If the product $\lambda^a w$ belongs to the $\mathbb{Q}$-subalgebra of `LaurentSeries ℚ` generated by the single element $\lambda$, that is, if $\lambda^a w$ is a polynomial in $\lambda$ with rational coefficients, then $w$ itself belongs to that subalgebra, i.e. $w$ is a polynomial in $\lambda$ with rational coefficients.
--
--   This is the cancellation step in the control of poles at the cusp $\infty$: since $\lambda \in \mathfrak q + \mathfrak q^2\mathbb{Q}[[\mathfrak q]]$, a power of $\lambda$ may be divided out of a polynomial in $\lambda$ provided the quotient has no negative-degree terms. It is used in [`ModularCurve.minpoly_lambdaNModC_coeff_mem_adjoin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.minpoly_lambdaNModC_coeff_mem_adjoin), where the coefficients of a minimal polynomial of a transformed $\lambda$-series are shown to be polynomials in $\lambda$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_mem_adjoin_lambdaModC_of_pow_mul_mem.lean

